y - 1 + \\pi\\rangle=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723026}] [{:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 0,1\\rangle\\cdot\\langle x - 1,y - 1\\rangle=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723027}] [{:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 0,1\\rangle\\cdot\\langle x + 2,y\\rangle=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723028}] [{:answer/feedback "This is $\\mathbf f^{\\prime}(u(t))$. Multiply all components by $u^{\\prime}(t)=2$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4t-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723082}] [{:answer/feedback "This is $\\mathbf g^{\\prime}(1/2)$. It still needs the multiplier $u^{\\prime}(\\ln 2)=-1/2$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723085}] [{:answer/feedback "The derivative of the constant third component is $0$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 8t-4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723087}] [{:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{t}{1+t^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723088}] [{:answer/feedback "The reciprocal derivative is negative, and $u^{\\prime}(\\ln 2)$ is also negative. Their product is positive." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1/2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723090}] [{:answer/feedback "Evaluate the outer derivative at $u(\\ln 2)=1/2$, then multiply every component by $-1/2$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1/2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723091}] [{:answer/feedback "The inner derivative is $-e^{-t}$, so the common multiplier is $-1/2$, not $1/2$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1/2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723094}] [{:answer/feedba